    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">IAP301 · Assessments</span>\n<h2>When you are tested</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">IAP301 · Kiểm tra & thi</span>\n<h2>Khi nào bị kiểm tra</h2></div>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Session<br><small>Buổi</small></th><th>Topic<br><small>Nội dung</small></th><th>LO</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>Assignment 1: Security Policies Overcoming Business Challenges</td><td>LO1</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>Lab 1: Craft an Organization-Wide Security Management Policy for Acceptable Use</td><td>LO1</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>Lab 1: Craft an Organization-Wide Security Management Policy for Acceptable Use (cont)</td><td>LO1</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>10</strong></td><td>Assignment 2: Good Policy Implementation</td><td>LO2</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>11</strong></td><td>Assignment 2: Good Policy Implementation (cont)</td><td>LO2</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>13</strong></td><td>Lab 2: Develop an Organization-Wide Policy Framework Implementation Plan</td><td>LO2</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>14</strong></td><td>Lab 2: Develop an Organization-Wide Policy Framework Implementation Plan (cont)</td><td>LO2</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>18</strong></td><td>Assignment 3: Security Policy Frameworks</td><td>LO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>19</strong></td><td>Lab 3: Define an Information Systems Security Policy Framework for an IT Infrastructure</td><td>LO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>20</strong></td><td>Lab 3: Define an Information Systems Security Policy Framework for an IT Infrastructure</td><td>LO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>24</strong></td><td>Assignment 4: Security Policy Creation</td><td>LO4</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>25</strong></td><td>Lab 4: Craft a Layered Security Management Policy - Separation of Duties</td><td>LO4</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>26</strong></td><td>Lab 4: Craft a Layered Security Management Policy - Separation of Duties (cont)</td><td>LO4</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>30</strong></td><td>Assignment 5: Create User Policy<br><br>Assigned Reading: - Ultrasound theft results in data breach at health care company Kaiser Permanente, Second Circuit rules in favor of Microsoft, gov't can't force access to email on Irish server (SC Magazine, July 2016)<br><br>- Office of Budget and Management: Federal Cybersecurity Workforce Strategy (July 2016)</td><td>LO5</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>31</strong></td><td>Lab 5: Craft an Organization-Wide Security Awareness Policy</td><td>LO5</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>32</strong></td><td>Lab 5: Craft an Organization-Wide Security Awareness Policy (cont)</td><td>LO5</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>33</strong></td><td>Review for Midterm</td><td>LO1, LO2, LO3, LO4, LO5</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>34</strong></td><td>Midterm Progress Test</td><td>LO1, LO2, LO3, LO4, LO5</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>38</strong></td><td>Assignment 6: IT Infrastructure Policies<br><br>Assigned Reading: Cyber Attack on Ukrainian Power Grid</td><td>LO6</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>39</strong></td><td>Lab 6: Define a Remote Access Policy to Support Remote Healthcare Clinics</td><td>LO6</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>40</strong></td><td>Lab 6: Define a Remote Access Policy to Support Remote Healthcare Clinics (cont)</td><td>LO6</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>42</strong></td><td>Assignment 7: Risk Management in a Business Model</td><td>LO7</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>43</strong></td><td>Lab 7: Identify Necessary Policies for Business Continuity – BIA &amp; Recovery Time Objectives, Focusing on Three Additional Security Requirements Identified in ref.[3]:<br><br>Incident Response (3.6), Risk Assessment (3.11), Security Assessment (3.12)</td><td>LO7</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>44</strong></td><td>Lab 7: Identify Necessary Policies for Business Continuity – BIA &amp; Recovery Time Objectives, Focusing on Three Additional Security (cont) Requirements Identified in ref.[3]:<br><br>Incident Response (3.6), Risk Assessment (3.11), Security Assessment (3.12)</td><td>LO7</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>47</strong></td><td>Lab 8: Craft a Security or Computer Incident Response Policy – CIRT Response Team</td><td>LO8</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>48</strong></td><td>Lab 8: Craft a Security or Computer Incident Response Policy – CIRT Response Team (cont)</td><td>LO8</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>50</strong></td><td>Assignment 9: Policy Monitoring and Enforcement Strategy</td><td>LO9</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>51</strong></td><td>Lab 9: Assess and Audit an Existing IT Security Policy Framework Definition</td><td>LO9</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>52</strong></td><td>Lab 9: Assess and Audit an Existing IT Security Policy Framework Definition (cont)</td><td>LO9</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>54</strong></td><td>Assignment 10: Automated Policy Compliance Systems (Software Evaluation Criteria spreadsheet)<br><br>Assigned Reading: Ransomware as a service business booming and growing, Settlement expected for 50M Home Depot customers (SC Magazine, Aug. 2016)</td><td>LO10</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>55</strong></td><td>Lab 10: Align an IT Security Policy Framework to the 7 Domains of a Typical IT Infrastructure</td><td>LO10</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>56</strong></td><td>Lab 10: Align an IT Security Policy Framework to the 7 Domains of a Typical IT Infrastructure (cont)</td><td>LO10</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>57</strong></td><td>Group Assignment Presentation: a Topic Chosen among 10 Discussions and Assignments</td><td>LO1, LO2, LO3, LO4, LO5, LO6, LO7, LO8, LO9, LO10</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>58</strong></td><td>Group Assignment Presentation: a Topic Chosen among 10 Discussions and Assignments (cont)</td><td>LO1, LO2, LO3, LO4, LO5, LO6, LO7, LO8, LO9, LO10</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>59</strong></td><td>Course Review</td><td>LO1, LO2, LO3, LO4, LO5, LO6, LO7, LO8, LO9, LO10</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>60</strong></td><td>Course Review (cont)</td><td>LO1, LO2, LO3, LO4, LO5, LO6, LO7, LO8, LO9, LO10</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>"
